  "description": "DELIBERATELY WRONG copy used by test-shared-fixtures-break.sh. MemoryPolicy.decide(event, codeKnown, current): whether a box save remembers its name and category as the named product of its code. event.kind: added (before is null), changed (box edit) or sessionCorrected (correction in the scan session list); after is the saved box (gtin, name, category, categoryOverridden). codeKnown: true = the reference names the code, false = it does not, null = the reference is unavailable or the lookup failed (cannot tell). current: the live named product of the code or null. expect.action none = nothing is written; remember = create or update the live named product with these values. A GTIN-less box and a known or undecidable code never remember. A change that touches neither the name nor the category (nor its flag) never remembers, so it cannot bring a forgotten product back.",
